{
  "_help": {
    "def_id": "Sycope alert definition id. An alert is matched to its profile by this id (definitionId / alertDefId in the webhook). Must be unique.",
    "rule_id": "Rule id of the definition (template library). Used only when the webhook has no definition id and exactly one profile has this rule id.",
    "name": "Definition name. Shown on the queue and status pages next to the job; not used for matching.",
    "time_range_s": "CHANGES THE WINDOW. Seconds the definition looks back (its timeRange). An alert at T is extracted from T - time_range_s - SR_EXPORTER_LAG_SECONDS to T + SR_WINDOW_MARGIN_SECONDS. 1 to 604800.",
    "packet_dims": "CHANGES THE BPF FILTER. Grouping fields of the definition that exist in packets: {field, alias} with field one of clientIp, serverIp, serverPort, protocol. Each one present in the alert becomes a term: host <clientIp>, host <serverIp>, port <serverPort>, <protocol>. Remove one to make the filter broader; an empty list with no static means NO BPF FILTER.",
    "static": "CHANGES THE BPF FILTER. Constant pre-filters of the definition: {\"serverPort\": [53]} or {\"protocol\": [17]}. Used when the port or protocol is not in packet_dims: one protocol -> udp/tcp/icmp, several ports -> (port a or port b). Several protocols add no term."
  },
  "format": 2,
